    ],
    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vacp2p/zerokit/tarball/v2.0.2",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vacp2p/zerokit/zipball/v2.0.2",
    "body": "# Zerokit v2.0.2 Release Notes\r\n\r\n## Highlights\r\n\r\nThis patch release closes a long-standing asymmetry in the RLN FFI surface and unblocks downstream consumers building on top of v2.0.1. `FFI_RLNProof` and `FFI_RLNProofValues` previously exposed `_get_*` accessors for every field but no constructors, forcing callers that decompose proofs into structs (e.g. `waku-rln-relay`) to hand-assemble the 290-byte wire layout and round-trip through `ffi_bytes_le_to_rln_proof`. New `ffi_rln_proof_new` and `ffi_rln_proof_values_new` constructors restore the missing direction so downstream code can build proofs the same way it tears them down.\r\n\r\nThe release also refreshes the Nix build inputs. The v2.0.1 tag shipped with a stale `cargoHash` in `nix/default.nix`; cold Nix builds failed with a hash mismatch because the cache-served fixed-output derivation masked the problem in CI. The hash has been regenerated and verified against `logos-delivery`'s downstream override.\r\n\r\nFinally, a redundant `.into_iter()` in `pm_tree_adapter::set_range` that newer clippy flags as `useless_conversion` has been removed — it was blocking CI on the default and `multi-message-id` builds.\r\n\r\n`FFI_RLNPartialProof` was deliberately *not* given a `_new` constructor: it has no field accessors either, so there is no symmetry gap to close. The only construction path remains `ffi_bytes_le_to_rln_partial_proof`.\r\n\r\n## What's New\r\n\r\n### Features\r\n- **feat(rln): add `ffi_rln_proof_new` and `ffi_rln_proof_values_new` constructors** ([#413](https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/413))\r\n  Closes the asymmetry in the FFI proof types. Downstream consumers that decompose proofs into structs can now reconstruct them without manually serializing the 290-byte wire layout. Three new tests cover the round-trip and invalid-input paths: `test_ffi_rln_proof_new_roundtrip`, `test_ffi_rln_proof_new_invalid_groth16_bytes`, `test_ffi_rln_proof_values_new_roundtrip`. Generated `rln.h` (via `--features headers`) now includes both functions.\r\n\r\n### Bug Fixes\r\n- **fix(nix): refresh `nix/default.nix` cargoHash** ([#413](https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/413))\r\n  Regenerates the fixed-output derivation hash that went stale on the v2.0.1 tag. Cold `nix build .#rln` now succeeds without a hash-mismatch error. Verified against `logos-delivery`'s downstream override.\r\n- **fix(rln): drop redundant `.into_iter()` in `pm_tree_adapter::set_range`** ([#413](https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/413))\r\n  Newer clippy flags this as `useless_conversion`. Unblocks `cargo clippy --all-targets --tests --release -- -D warnings` on default and `multi-message-id` feature builds.\r\n\r\n## Version Matrix\r\n\r\n| Crate          | Version | Change    |\r\n|----------------|---------|-----------|\r\n| rln            | 2.0.2   | patch     |\r\n| zerokit_utils  | 1.2.0   | unchanged |\r\n| rln-wasm       | 2.0.1   | unchanged |\r\n| rln-cli        | 0.6.0   | unchanged |\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n* chore(release): v2.0.2 by @seemenkina in https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/413\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/compare/v2.0.1...v2.0.2\r\n",
    "mentions_count": 1
  },
