    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vacp2p/zerokit/tarball/v2.0.1",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vacp2p/zerokit/zipball/v2.0.1",
    "body": "# Zerokit v2.0.1 Release Notes\r\n\r\n## Highlights\r\n\r\nThis patch release simplifies the hash function API across the entire zerokit stack. The Poseidon hash and Keccak-based `hash_to_field` functions can never actually fail for valid inputs (the only error case was an input-length mismatch against hardcoded round parameters), so the `Result` wrapping was unnecessary ceremony that leaked into every caller. By removing it, the API is cleaner, call sites require fewer `?` operators and `.unwrap()` calls, and the FFI layer returns values directly instead of `CResult` wrappers.\r\n\r\nThe `Hasher` trait in `zerokit_utils` was also simplified: the associated `Error` type was removed, and the generic `hash(&[Fr])` method was replaced with the more specific `hash_pair(left, right)` since Merkle trees only ever hash pairs of nodes. A fallible `poseidon_hash_try_from()` function is still available for callers who need runtime input-length validation.\r\n\r\nThe release also fixes the Docs.rs build (which failed for v2.0.0 because `all-features = true` activated mutually exclusive feature flags) and resolves a CI breakage where a pinned git revision of the `cross` tool was incompatible with newer Rust toolchains.\r\n\r\n## What's New\r\n\r\n### Bug Fixes\r\n- **fix: remove Result from hash to field functions** ([#398](https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/398))\r\n  Simplified `poseidon_hash`, `hash_to_field_le/be`, keygen functions, FFI functions, and WASM bindings to return values directly instead of `Result`. Removed `HashError`, `zerokit_utils::error` module, and `Hasher::Error` associated type. Extracted `RecoverSecretError` from `ProtocolError` for more precise slashing error handling.\r\n- **fix(doc): address failed Docs.rs build** ([#397](https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/397))\r\n  Changed `package.metadata.docs.rs` from `all-features = true` to explicit feature list because mutually exclusive feature flags caused the docs.rs build to fail.\r\n\r\n### Chores\r\n- **chore: update dependencies and version for rln crate to 2.0.1** ([#401](https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/401))\r\n  Version bumps, fixed `cross` CI installation (pinned git rev -> released v0.2.5), fixed cargo doc warnings.\r\n\r\n## Version Matrix\r\n\r\n| Crate | Version | Change |\r\n|-------|---------|--------|\r\n| rln | 2.0.1 | patch |\r\n| zerokit_utils | 1.2.0 | minor |\r\n| rln-wasm | 2.0.1 | patch |\r\n| rln-cli | 0.6.0 | unchanged |\r\n\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n* fix(doc): address failed Docs.rs build for v2.0.1 patch by @vinhtc27 in https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/397\r\n* fix: remove Result from hash to field functions for v2.0.1 patch by @vinhtc27 in https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/398\r\n* chore: update dependencies and version for rln crate to 2.0.1 by @seemenkina in https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/401\r\n* chore: bump version for utils and update lock files by @seemenkina in https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/pull/402\r\n\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/vacp2p/zerokit/compare/v2.0.0...v2.0.1",
    "mentions_count": 2
  },
